\u003Cimg title=\"I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2018-07-06\" src=\"ISic000306_copy2_tiled-thumb.tif\">\u003C/a>\u003Ca href=\"ISic000306_copy2.jpg\">\u003Cimg title=\"I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2018-07-06\" src=\"ISic000306_copy2-thumb.jpg\">\u003C/a>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"apparatus\">\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cp>  \u003C/p>\u003Cp>  \u003C/p>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">  \u003C/p>\u003Cp>consul (?)\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2>Italian translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">  \u003C/p>\u003Cp>  \u003C/p>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"commentary\">\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>See \u003Ca href=\"http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic003159\" target=\"_blank\">ISic003159\u003C/a>for the text on the reverse. The interpretation is very uncertain, whether the text is incomplete and whether CONS stands for consul (but not the usual abbreviation thereof), or the first part of a name such as Considius (suggested by Manganaro). Mommsen speculated that, given the reverse has a (later) text with the word 'fines', it should be paralleled with CIL X.7232 from Marsala (fines inter Vandalos...), but Manganaro and Korhonen both consider this text to be earlier and not necessarily in any way connected to the text on the reverse. A terminus of some sort (rather than a milestone) seems possible (fullest discussion in Manganaro).\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"bibliography\">\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Gualtherus 1624 [1625] 54 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001931\